Subject: [PATCH] VAAPI: retire processed accounting before publishing PICTURE

The decoder may consume PICTURE and start its next drain before the output
thread returns from SendInMessage. Transfer the processed count first while
the render count still covers the picture, including the publication boundary.

Upstream-Source: https://github.com/xbmc/xbmc/blob/a3a448d26b8d560a65655dab2cd122994dc4e146/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/VAAPI.cpp
Base-Revision: a3a448d26b8d560a65655dab2cd122994dc4e146
Source-SHA256: 6239d286046bbc0b8c724f78cce5409278cbb56c0a4d8ee306f6738f3353de38
Copyright: Copyright (C) 2005-2018 Team Kodi
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later

--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/VAAPI.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/VAAPI.cpp
@@ -1808,12 +1808,13 @@
             procPic = m_bufferPool->processedPics.front();
             m_bufferPool->processedPics.pop_front();
             outPic = ProcessPicture(procPic);
+            // Transfer accounting before publication: the decoder may consume
+            // PICTURE and start its next drain before SendInMessage returns.
             if (outPic)
-            {
               m_config.stats->IncRender();
+            m_config.stats->DecProcessed();
+            if (outPic)
               m_dataPort.SendInMessage(COutputDataProtocol::PICTURE, &outPic, sizeof(outPic));
-            }
-            m_config.stats->DecProcessed();
           }
           m_state = O_TOP_CONFIGURED_IDLE;
           m_extTimeout = 0ms;
